# Conventions

The three conventions every part of the factory shares, so a worker, the
coordinator, the verifier and the website compute the same numbers.

Money is an `Int` of MICRO-DOLLARS: one dollar is 1,000,000, so a budget check is
integer comparison and a ledger sums exactly. Scores are `Int`s in BASIS POINTS
of their scale: 10,000 is the top, a probability of 0.4 is 4,000 and a score of
5.4 out of 10 is 5,400. Time is an `Int` of Unix milliseconds, what `now()`
answers. And every hash is `sha256Hex`, so hashes agree by construction.

## Note
The lowercase hex SHA-256 of a text's UTF-8 bytes.

## To sha256Hex (t: Text) -> Text:
    Return bytesToHex(sha256(text_bytes(t))).

## Note
Micro-dollars as a reader expects money, all six decimals kept: a cost rounded
for display is a cost that no longer adds up.

## To formatMicros (micros: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable sign be "".
    Let mutable n be micros.
    If micros is less than 0:
        Set sign to "-".
        Set n to 0 - micros.
    Return sign + "$" + "{n / 1000000}" + "." + zfill("{n % 1000000}", 6).

## Note
Lines joined into one text, one element a line. A multi-line literal inside an
indented block is misread once a program reaches `crypto.lg` (see
`LOGOS_ISSUES.md`, issue 7), so a text of several lines is written as its lines.

## To joinLines (xs: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Return join(xs, "\n").

## Note
A text safe as one path segment: the factory's ids hold colons and slashes.

## To slugOf (id: Text) -> Text:
    Return replace(replace(id, ":", "_"), "/", "_").

## Test: SHA-256 of abc is the FIPS vector

Expect that sha256Hex("abc") is equal to "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad".
Expect that length of sha256Hex("") is equal to 64.

## Test: money prints with all six decimals

Expect that formatMicros(0) is equal to "$0.000000".
Expect that formatMicros(1250) is equal to "$0.001250".
Expect that formatMicros(5000000) is equal to "$5.000000".
Expect that formatMicros(1234567) is equal to "$1.234567".
Expect that formatMicros(0 - 42) is equal to "-$0.000042".

## Test: lines join with newlines and ids become path segments

Expect that joinLines(["a", "", "b"]) is equal to "a\n\nb".
Expect that slugOf("op:OP022") is equal to "op_OP022".
Expect that slugOf("fc:Arxiv/0912.2382/Curling") is equal to "fc_Arxiv_0912.2382_Curling".

## Test: a cost and its negation print the same digits

For all booleans b:
    Let mutable n be 1250.
    If b:
        Set n to 5000000.
    Expect that formatMicros(0 - n) is equal to "-" + formatMicros(n).
